# ── Weather provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to Open-Meteo (free, no key required). Only set these to switch.
# VITE_WEATHER_PROVIDER=open-meteo
# VITE_WEATHER_PROVIDER=weatherapi   (requires VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY)
# VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY=

# ── Firebase (Firestore) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All four vars are required to activate Firestore sync.
# Without them the app works fully — data stays in localStorage only.
#
# MVP NOTE: The app uses Firestore keyed by normalized email address (no Firebase
# Auth). This is intentional for closed beta. For public launch, enable Firebase
# Auth and update Firestore security rules to enforce ownership by email.
# See src/lib/cloudSync.ts for the security comment in the Firestore path.
#
# Firestore security rules for MVP (open — trusted users only):
#   rules_version = '2';
#   service cloud.firestore {
#     match /databases/{database}/documents {
#       match /users/{emailKey}/{document=**} {
#         allow read, write: if true;
#       }
#     }
#   }
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN:
#   LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: use the default Firebase domain, e.g. wethra-1aa65.firebaseapp.com
#   PRODUCTION (www.aeruvo.app): MUST be set to www.aeruvo.app
#     This is required for signInWithRedirect to work in Safari 16.1+, Firefox 109+,
#     and Chrome with third-party cookie blocking. The Vercel rewrite in vercel.json
#     proxies https://www.aeruvo.app/__/auth/** to the Firebase auth helper endpoints.
#     Do NOT set this to www.aeruvo.app without the vercel.json rewrite in place.
#     See: https://firebase.google.com/docs/auth/web/redirect-best-practices
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=   # from Firebase Console → Project Settings → Cloud Messaging
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Notifications (Stage D+) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for Firebase Cloud Messaging (Web Push) push notifications.
# VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY is the Web Push certificate PUBLIC key from:
#   Firebase Console → Project Settings → Cloud Messaging → Web Push certificates
# This is safe to commit — it is a public key, not a secret.
# Note: messagingSenderId is part of the standard Firebase config (VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID
# etc.) and does NOT need a separate VITE_* var.
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=
#
# Show notification opt-in UI (Stage C/D). Hidden in production until
# Stage E (Cloud Function scheduler) is deployed and tested.
# VITE_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=true

# ── Stripe ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_ prefix = safe to expose in client bundle (publishable key only).
# Non-VITE_ vars = server-only, NEVER in client code or VITE_ variables.
#
# Client-side (safe):
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
#
# Server-only (NEVER commit, NEVER use VITE_ prefix):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_PREMIUM_PRICE_ID=price_...
#
# Firebase Admin (server-only — stringified JSON of service account):
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT={"type":"service_account","project_id":"wethra-1aa65",...}

# ── Wardrobe AI (Gemini) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. NEVER use VITE_ prefix for any of these variables.
#
# WARDROBE_AI_SCANNING_ENABLED: Master on/off switch for AI wardrobe scanning.
#   Set to "true" in production only when a Paid Gemini project is configured
#   and the feature is ready for users.
#   When "false" (or absent in production), scanning returns a friendly
#   "temporarily unavailable" message — no quota reservation, no Gemini call.
#   In development, omitting this variable defaults to enabled.
# WARDROBE_AI_SCANNING_ENABLED=false
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY: API key for the Google Gemini project (Paid project in production).
#   In production this must be a Paid Services API key.
#   Personal data must not be submitted using an Unpaid/Free tier key.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
#
# GEMINI_SERVICE_TIER: Must be set to "paid" in production.
#   Wardrobe scanning is disabled if this is missing or not "paid".
#   In development/staging, set to "development" to enable local testing.
#   Do not commit actual keys or set this to "paid" unless using a Paid project.
# GEMINI_SERVICE_TIER=paid
#
# GEMINI_WARDROBE_MODEL: Gemini model for wardrobe analysis.
#   Default: gemini-3.6-flash. Change only after accuracy/cost testing.
# GEMINI_WARDROBE_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
#
# Scan quota limits are policy-locked constants defined in src/lib/policyVersions.ts
# (POLICY_FREE_LIFETIME_SCANS=3, POLICY_PREMIUM_DAILY_SCANS=15, POLICY_PREMIUM_ROLLING_SCANS=100).
# They are NOT configurable via environment variables in production.
# Production startup fails if code constants do not match these policy values.

# ── Production origin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required in production. Must be an https://aeruvo.app origin.
# AERUVO_ORIGIN=https://aeruvo.app
